        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>MySQL</strong></td>
        <td>Network-bound</td>
        <td>Network-bound</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Memory and SQLite stores run synchronously on Bun's main thread, avoiding
    Promise overhead entirely. Redis and Postgres require network I/O, so they return Promises.
    Choose based on whether you need persistence or distribution.
  </p>
